 "spin_inferred": "Follow (top), struck hard, with at most a trace of side. Why: the brown is hit about three-quarter ball at 4.1 m/s and the cue ball leaves near the tangent line at 1.1 m/s, then bends forward and speeds up to 1.5 m/s over the next 0.5 s. A ball rolling naturally at contact ends with 2/7 of its speed along the line of centres plus its tangent speed, here 1.55 m/s at 174 degrees; measured 1.47 m/s at 173 as it reaches the cushion. A centre-ball hit would have had only about half that roll after 1.4 m at this pace, so the cue ball was struck above centre. Stun would have left it near the brown spot and screw would have brought it back. Side: it meets the baulk cushion 7 degrees off square and leaves 2 degrees off square on the same side (speed along the cushion 0.18 in, 0.04 out); that narrowing could be a little left-hand (check) side or just the cushion, so side is not established.",
